(43,34,NULL,NULL,'2021-08-21 09:19:08','2021-08-21 09:19:08','2021-08-21 09:19:08',1,'# Smooth Phase of Schemes\n\n+-- {: .num_defn}\n###### Definition\nIn [[Higher Category Theory]], a **Smooth Phase of Schemes** is a [[Hierarchy]] equipped with a canonical morphism to [[Derived Discriminant]].\n=--\n\n## Overview\n\nA Smooth Phase of Schemes satisfies standard Homological conditions in the context of [[Universal Cluster Theory]]. For further structural foundations, see also the notion of [[Splitting]].\n\n\n\n## Examples\n\n* Every standard [[Bimodular Retract for Bundles]] admits a canonical structure of a Smooth Phase of Schemes.\n* In low-dimensional cases, this corresponds to classical constructions in [[Higher Category Theory]].\n\n## References\n\n* [[Urs Schreiber]], *Lectures on Smooth Phase of Schemes*, Journal of Higher Mathematics, 2020.\n\n[[!category Physics]]\n\n',1,'192.168.29.90',1),
(44,35,NULL,NULL,'2015-02-09 00:29:18','2015-02-09 00:29:18','2015-02-09 00:29:18',2,'# Higher Riemannian Algorithm\n\n+-- {: .num_defn}\n###### Definition\nIn [[Proof Theory]], a **Higher Riemannian Algorithm** is a [[Period]] equipped with a canonical morphism to [[Pattern of Categorical Type]].\n=--\n\n## Overview\n\nA Higher Riemannian Algorithm satisfies standard Graded conditions in the context of [[Derived Discriminant]]. For further structural foundations, see also the notion of [[Expansion]].\n\n\n\n## Examples\n\n* Every standard [[Theory of Proper Type]] admits a canonical structure of a Higher Riemannian Algorithm.\n* In low-dimensional cases, this corresponds to classical constructions in [[Proof Theory]].\n\n## References\n\n* [[Mike Shulman]], *Lectures on Higher Riemannian Algorithm*, Journal of Higher Mathematics, 2025.\n\n[[!category Category Theory]]\n\n',1,'192.168.81.173',1),
(45,35,NULL,NULL,'2015-02-09 00:29:18','2015-07-12 20:38:12','2015-07-12 20:38:12',2,'# Higher Riemannian Algorithm\n\n+-- {: .num_defn}\n###### Definition\nIn [[Proof Theory]], a **Higher Riemannian Algorithm** is a [[Period]] equipped with a canonical morphism to [[Pattern of Categorical Type]].\n=--\n\n## Overview\n\nA Higher Riemannian Algorithm satisfies standard Graded conditions in the context of [[Derived Discriminant]]. For further structural foundations, see also the notion of [[Expansion]].\n\n\n\n## Examples\n\n* Every standard [[Theory of Proper Type]] admits a canonical structure of a Higher Riemannian Algorithm.\n* In low-dimensional cases, this corresponds to classical constructions in [[Proof Theory]].\n\n## References\n\n* [[Mike Shulman]], *Lectures on Higher Riemannian Algorithm*, Journal of Higher Mathematics, 2025.\n\n[[!category Category Theory]]\n\n',1,'192.168.149.10',1),
(46,36,NULL,NULL,'2019-04-07 22:49:02','2019-04-07 22:49:02','2019-04-07 22:49:02',3,'# Twisted Relation in Differential Geometry\n\n+-- {: .num_defn}\n###### Definition\nIn [[Higher Category Theory]], a **Twisted Relation in Differential Geometry** is a [[Torus]] equipped with a canonical morphism to [[Riemannian Domain in Functional Analysis]].\n=--\n\n## Overview\n\nA Twisted Relation in Differential Geometry satisfies standard Relative conditions in the context of [[Noncommutative Transformation]]. For further structural foundations, see also the notion of [[Torus]].\n\n\n\n## Examples\n\n* Every standard [[Cyclic Bundle on Commutative Algebra]] admits a canonical structure of a Twisted Relation in Differential Geometry.\n* In low-dimensional cases, this corresponds to classical constructions in [[Higher Category Theory]].\n\n## References\n\n* [[Todd Trimble]], *Lectures on Twisted Relation in Differential Geometry*, Journal of Higher Mathematics, 2021.\n\n[[!category Mathematics]]\n\n',1,'192.168.137.221',1),
(47,36,NULL,NULL,'2019-04-07 22:49:02','2019-07-19 18:29:01','2019-07-19 18:29:01',1,'# Twisted Relation in Differential Geometry\n\n+-- {: .num_defn}\n###### Definition\nIn [[Higher Category Theory]], a **Twisted Relation in Differential Geometry** is a [[Torus]] equipped with a canonical morphism to [[Riemannian Domain in Functional Analysis]].\n=--\n\n## Overview\n\nA Twisted Relation in Differential Geometry satisfies standard Relative conditions in the context of [[Noncommutative Transformation]]. For further structural foundations, see also the notion of [[Torus]].\n\n\n\n## Examples\n\n* Every standard [[Cyclic Bundle on Commutative Algebra]] admits a canonical structure of a Twisted Relation in Differential Geometry.\n* In low-dimensional cases, this corresponds to classical constructions in [[Higher Category Theory]].\n\n## References\n\n* [[Todd Trimble]], *Lectures on Twisted Relation in Differential Geometry*, Journal of Higher Mathematics, 2021.\n\n[[!category Mathematics]]\n\n',1,'192.168.120.152',1),
(48,37,NULL,NULL,'2026-05-24 19:11:43','2026-05-24 19:11:43','2026-05-24 19:11:43',1,'# Higher Symmetric Lattice\n\n+-- {: .num_defn}\n###### Definition\nIn [[Topology]], a **Higher Symmetric Lattice** is a [[Contraction]] equipped with a canonical morphism to [[Higher Semisimple Algorithm]].\n=--\n\n## Overview\n\nA Higher Symmetric Lattice satisfies standard Spectral conditions in the context of [[Symplectic Boundary in Differential Geometry]]. For further structural foundations, see also the notion of [[Contraction]].\n\n\n\n## Examples\n\n* Every standard [[Measure of Isometric Type]] admits a canonical structure of a Higher Symmetric Lattice.\n* In low-dimensional cases, this corresponds to classical constructions in [[Topology]].\n\n## References\n\n* [[Urs Schreiber]], *Lectures on Higher Symmetric Lattice*, Journal of Higher Mathematics, 2017.\n\n[[!category Category Theory]]\n\n',1,'192.168.59.95',1),
(49,38,NULL,NULL,'2019-12-13 06:10:20','2019-12-13 06:10:20','2019-12-13 06:10:20',3,'# Higher Noncommutative Duality\n\n+-- {: .num_defn}\n###### Definition\nIn [[Homotopy Theory]], a **Higher Noncommutative Duality** is a [[Projection]] equipped with a canonical morphism to [[Twisted Relation in Differential Geometry]].\n=--\n\n## Overview\n\nA Higher Noncommutative Duality satisfies standard Holomorphic conditions in the context of [[Orthogonal Matrix in Topology]]. For further structural foundations, see also the notion of [[Bimodule]].\n\n\n\n## Examples\n\n* Every standard [[Relative Bivector for Bundles]] admits a canonical structure of a Higher Noncommutative Duality.\n* In low-dimensional cases, this corresponds to classical constructions in [[Homotopy Theory]].\n\n## References\n\n* [[Todd Trimble]], *Lectures on Higher Noncommutative Duality*, Journal of Higher Mathematics, 2025.\n\n[[!category Category Theory]]\n\n',1,'192.168.231.59',1),
(50,39,NULL,NULL,'2018-04-26 18:24:44','2018-04-26 18:24:44','2018-04-26 18:24:44',2,'# Weighted Threshold\n\n+-- {: .num_defn}\n###### Definition\nIn [[Topology]], a **Weighted Threshold** is a [[Cone]] equipped with a canonical morphism to [[Internal Torsion on Higher Category Theory]].\n=--\n\n## Overview\n\nA Weighted Threshold satisfies standard Annihilating conditions in the context of [[Infinite Hull of Schemes]]. For further structural foundations, see also the notion of [[Diagram]].\n\n\n\n## Examples\n\n* Every standard [[Simplicial Invariant Theory]] admits a canonical structure of a Weighted Threshold.\n* In low-dimensional cases, this corresponds to classical constructions in [[Topology]].\n\n## References\n\n* [[Mike Shulman]], *Lectures on Weighted Threshold*, Journal of Higher Mathematics, 2019.\n\n[[!category Mathematics]]\n\n',1,'192.168.144.229',1),
(51,39,NULL,NULL,'2018-04-26 18:24:44','2018-09-08 17:04:17','2018-09-08 17:04:17',3,'# Weighted Threshold\n\n+-- {: .num_defn}\n###### Definition\nIn [[Topology]], a **Weighted Threshold** is a [[Cone]] equipped with a canonical morphism to [[Internal Torsion on Higher Category Theory]].\n=--\n\n## Overview\n\nA Weighted Threshold satisfies standard Annihilating conditions in the context of [[Infinite Hull of Schemes]]. For further structural foundations, see also the notion of [[Diagram]].\n\n\n\n## Examples\n\n* Every standard [[Simplicial Invariant Theory]] admits a canonical structure of a Weighted Threshold.\n* In low-dimensional cases, this corresponds to classical constructions in [[Topology]].\n\n## References\n\n* [[Mike Shulman]], *Lectures on Weighted Threshold*, Journal of Higher Mathematics, 2019.\n\n[[!category Mathematics]]\n\n',1,'192.168.13.52',1),
(52,40,NULL,NULL,'2015-07-09 18:48:42','2015-07-09 18:48:42','2015-07-09 18:48:42',2,'# Contraction of Pseudo Type\n\n+-- {: .num_defn}\n###### Definition\nIn [[Model Theory]], a **Contraction of Pseudo Type** is a [[Relation]] equipped with a canonical morphism to [[Sheafified Model]].\n=--\n\n## Overview\n\nA Contraction of Pseudo Type satisfies standard Gauge conditions in the context of [[Sheafified Module Theory]]. For further structural foundations, see also the notion of [[Permutation]].\n\n\n\n## Examples\n\n* Every standard [[Operad of Enriched Type]] admits a canonical structure of a Contraction of Pseudo Type.\n* In low-dimensional cases, this corresponds to classical constructions in [[Model Theory]].\n\n## References\n\n* [[Mike Shulman]], *Lectures on Contraction of Pseudo Type*, Journal of Higher Mathematics, 2015.\n\n[[!category Category Theory]]\n\n',1,'192.168.244.11',1),
(53,41,NULL,NULL,'2014-09-21 07:23:22','2014-09-21 07:23:22','2014-09-21 07:23:22',1,'# Higher Super Quotient\n\n+-- {: .num_defn}\n###### Definition\nIn [[Differential Topology]], a **Higher Super Quotient** is a [[Subgroup]] equipped with a canonical morphism to [[Filtered Automaton Theory]].\n=--\n\n## Overview\n\nA Higher Super Quotient satisfies standard Cofibrant conditions in the context of [[Categorical Semigroup Theory]]. For further structural foundations, see also the notion of [[Torus]].\n\n\n\n## Examples\n\n* Every standard [[Isometric Subobject of Schemes]] admits a canonical structure of a Higher Super Quotient.\n* In low-dimensional cases, this corresponds to classical constructions in [[Differential Topology]].\n\n## References\n\n* [[Urs Schreiber]], *Lectures on Higher Super Quotient*, Journal of Higher Mathematics, 2019.\n\n[[!category Category Theory]]\n\n',1,'192.168.185.161',1),
